      <section class="section section-alt">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="portfolio-grid case-study-layout">
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Project Overview</span>
              <h2>What the system does and why teams depended on it</h2>
              <p>LeadFlow CRM is a saas platform built for sales and growth teams handling ongoing inbound lead volume. The product was designed to move teams away from fragmented lead handling into a structured, high-visibility CRM workflow.</p>
              <p>From an engineering perspective, the system had to process frequent inbound activity, routing changes, and active pipeline work across multiple users without stale data. That made it a production platform with real operational demands rather than a portfolio demo.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Business Challenge</span>
              <h2>What had to improve for the product to scale cleanly</h2>
              <p>The core business challenge was delivering a product that could serve CRM, lead operations, and sales enablement use cases while still remaining easy for operators to trust and use every day.</p>
              <p>The product needed to improve response speed, ownership clarity, and pipeline trust so growth teams could convert more demand into active opportunities.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Constraints &amp; Complexity</span>
              <h3>Engineering realities that shaped implementation choices</h3>
            </div>
            <p>The delivery had to solve product problems, operational risk, and scaling concerns at the same time.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-grid project-complexity-grid">
            
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Lead Volume</h3>
              <p>The system needed to process frequent inbound activity without slow filtering or stale pipeline views.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Ownership Clarity</h3>
              <p>Assignments and follow-up state had to be obvious for distributed sales teams.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Realtime Changes</h3>
              <p>Status changes and routing updates needed near-instant propagation.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Integration Readiness</h3>
              <p>Lead sources and communication channels had to stay adaptable over time.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-accent">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Solution Architecture</span>
              <h2>System design, integrations, and delivery approach</h2>
            </div>
            <p>The implementation emphasized maintainability, production-readiness, and cleaner operational workflows.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="case-study-hero architecture-layout">
            <article class="content-panel">
              <h3>Implementation approach</h3>
              <p>The solution used Laravel 12, Vue 3, Redis, WebSockets, MySQL, Pusher, social platform APIs across a modular application architecture. Core workflows were separated into clearer domain boundaries so business logic, integrations, and UI concerns did not become tightly coupled.</p>
              <p>That approach made the system easier to scale, easier to monitor, and easier to extend as new requirements appeared. It also created better release confidence for a product expected to handle real customer traffic and operator activity.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="content-panel architecture-diagram-panel">
              <span class="eyebrow">Architecture Diagram</span>
              <div class="architecture-diagram" aria-label="System architecture">
                <div class="arch-node">Operator UI</div>
                <div class="arch-arrow bi bi-arrow-down"></div>
                <div class="arch-node">Domain Services</div>
                <div class="arch-arrow bi bi-arrow-down"></div>
                <div class="arch-row">
                  <div class="arch-node small">Integrations</div>
                  <div class="arch-node small">Reporting</div>
                </div>
                <div class="arch-arrow bi bi-arrow-down"></div>
                <div class="arch-node">Primary Data Store</div>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Key Features</span>
              <h3>Product capabilities designed for business outcomes</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Every capability was selected because it made the platform more useful, more scalable, or easier to operate.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="services-grid">
            
            <article class="service-card">
              <i class="bi bi-funnel"></i>
              <h3>Lead Capture & Qualification</h3>
              <p>Turned inbound prospects into structured, reviewable lead records.</p>
              <span>Improved pipeline hygiene from the first touchpoint.</span>
            </article>
            <article class="service-card">
              <i class="bi bi-arrow-left-right"></i>
              <h3>Assignment & Routing</h3>
              <p>Applied ownership and workflow rules to move leads quickly to the right team members.</p>
              <span>Reduced lag in initial outreach.</span>
            </article>
            <article class="service-card">
              <i class="bi bi-lightning-charge"></i>
              <h3>Realtime Pipeline Updates</h3>
              <p>Broadcasted status and ownership changes to active users.</p>
              <span>Kept the sales floor aligned on what changed.</span>
            </article>
            <article class="service-card">
              <i class="bi bi-bar-chart-steps"></i>
              <h3>Pipeline Reporting</h3>
              <p>Tracked lead stage movement, throughput, and bottlenecks in one place.</p>
              <span>Made optimization decisions more evidence-based.</span>
            </article>
            <article class="service-card">
              <i class="bi bi-link-45deg"></i>
              <h3>Source Integration Readiness</h3>
              <p>Supported evolving inbound channels and external lead sources.</p>
              <span>Made the CRM more adaptable to growth strategies.</span>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-deep">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Performance &amp; Scalability</span>
              <h2>Technical decisions that improved stability and maintainability</h2>
            </div>
            <p>Architecture choices focused on safe growth, cleaner releases, and operational clarity.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-grid">
            
            <article class="feature-card">
              <h3>Asynchronous workflow handling</h3>
              <p><strong>Why chosen:</strong> The platform needed to support process frequent inbound activity, routing changes, and active pipeline work across multiple users without stale data without blocking the main user journey.</p>
              <p><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> This added queue, retry, and observability responsibilities to the architecture.</p>
              <span class="feature-meta"><strong>Outcome:</strong> Heavy tasks moved out of request-response flows, keeping the product faster and more stable.</span>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <h3>Service-layer integration boundaries</h3>
              <p><strong>Why chosen:</strong> The product relied on multiple external or subsystem workflows across CRM, lead operations, and sales enablement.</p>
              <p><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> More explicit service boundaries required extra design effort early in delivery.</p>
              <span class="feature-meta"><strong>Outcome:</strong> The codebase became safer to extend and easier to debug as the platform evolved.</span>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <h3>Domain-first product modeling</h3>
              <p><strong>Why chosen:</strong> The business needed stronger operational clarity around move teams away from fragmented lead handling into a structured, high-visibility CRM workflow.</p>
              <p><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> It took longer to model states and rules than a quick CRUD implementation would have.</p>
              <span class="feature-meta"><strong>Outcome:</strong> The result was a system with clearer workflows, better reporting, and lower long-term maintenance risk.</span>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Technologies Used</span>
              <h3>Production stack behind the platform</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Chosen to support maintainable delivery, good product performance, and cleaner operations.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stack-grid project-stack-minimal">
            <article class="stack-group"><h3>Frontend</h3><p>Vue 3, pipeline dashboards</p></article><article class="stack-group"><h3>Backend</h3><p>Laravel 12, routing services</p></article><article class="stack-group"><h3>Data</h3><p>MySQL, Redis</p></article><article class="stack-group"><h3>Infra</h3><p>WebSockets, Pusher</p></article><article class="stack-group"><h3>Integrations</h3><p>Lead sources, social platform APIs</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-alt">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Results &amp; Impact</span>
              <h2>Business outcomes supported by stronger engineering execution</h2>
            </div>
            <p>Metrics and operating improvements that made the product more effective and easier to scale.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stats-grid project-impact-metrics">
            <article class="stat-card"><strong>+28%</strong><span>Lead conversion improvement after routing and follow-up visibility upgrades</span></article><article class="stat-card"><strong>-43%</strong><span>Time lost to unclear lead ownership and stale pipeline data</span></article><article class="stat-card"><strong>2.6x</strong><span>Faster lead triage across active sales queues</span></article><article class="stat-card"><strong>99.9%</strong><span>Availability across CRM reporting and operator views</span></article>
          </div>
          <article class="content-panel result-points">
            <ul>
              <li>Improved sales execution with clearer routing and faster pipeline awareness.</li><li>Replaced fragmented lead handling with a structured CRM workflow.</li><li>Added realtime confidence to a product used continuously by active teams.</li><li>Strengthened positioning around SaaS systems and business operations platforms.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Related Projects</span>
              <h3>Adjacent systems with similar product and architecture depth</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Internal linking makes it easier to explore adjacent AI, SaaS, marketplace, and custom business platform work.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="portfolio-grid portfolio-grid-3">
            
            <article class="project-card project-card-detail">
